design:
Establish the square frame FIRST, then overlay the image and clip, instead of letting the image size the container. Pattern:

Color.lunara(.backgroundBase)
    .aspectRatio(1, contentMode: .fit)
    .overlay {
        AsyncImage(url: url) { image in
            image.resizable().scaledToFill()   // no inner .frame
        } placeholder: { ProgressView() }
    }
    .clipped()

The overlay is sized to the square base; scaledToFill overflows within that square; .clipped() reliably trims it. Drop the inner .frame(maxWidth:.infinity, maxHeight:.infinity) on the image. Consider extracting a single reusable SquareArtworkView since the pattern is copy-pasted across 8 views.
